.TH IAM\-SHRINK 1 "2026-09" "iam-shrink" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iam-shrink \- shrink IAM policies to what CloudTrail says is actually used
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iam-shrink
.B analyze
.I ROLE_NAME
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares the actions a role is allowed against the actions it has actually
used, and emits the smaller policy \(em as a report, as a policy document,
or as a Terraform diff.
.PP
Allowed actions come from the role's attached and inline policies. Used
actions come either from a pre-exported JSON of CloudTrail events, or from
an Athena query over CloudTrail Lake.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI analyze " ROLE_NAME"
Analyse one role.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-usage " FILE"
JSON file of CloudTrail events, as
.I [{eventSource, eventName}, ...]
.TP
.BI \-\-athena\-table " TABLE"
CloudTrail Lake table to query instead of
.BR \-\-usage .
Requires
.BR \-\-athena\-output .
.TP
.BI \-\-athena\-output " S3_URI"
S3 URI for Athena query results.
.TP
.BI \-\-athena\-days " N"
Lookback window in days.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
.BR report ,
.B policy
or
.B tf-diff
(default report).
.TP
.BI \-\-analyzer\-arn " ARN"
IAM Access Analyzer ARN. Cross-checks its unused-permission findings
against the CloudTrail-based result. Report format only, and requires
.BR \-\-role\-arn .
.TP
.BI \-\-role\-arn " ARN"
Role ARN to look up in Access Analyzer.
.TP
.B \-\-open\-pr
Commit the Terraform diff on a new branch and open a pull request with
.BR gh .
Run from inside the target infrastructure repository.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
An analysis was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
AWS could not be queried, or the arguments were rejected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
From an exported event history:
.PP
.RS
.B iam-shrink analyze deploy-role \-\-usage events.json
.RE
.PP
Straight to a reviewable Terraform change:
.PP
.RS
.B iam-shrink analyze deploy-role \-\-usage events.json \-\-format tf-diff
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cost-diff (1),
.BR idle-hunter (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/iam-shrink
.UE
